   344|    <!-- PAGE 4: ELEMENTAL ANALYSIS -->
   345|    <div class="page">
   346|        <div class="section-header">The Five Elements</div>
   347|        <div class="chapter-title">Your Elemental Balance</div>
   348|        
   349|        <p>
   350|            Your chart is composed of five elemental forces. Their relative strength tells me where your natural power lies — and what you must consciously cultivate.
   351|        </p>
   352|        
   353|        <table class="pillars-table" style="text-align: left;">
   354|            <tr style="background: var(--ink); color: white;">
   355|                <th style="text-align:left">Element</th>
   356|                <th style="text-align:left">Strength</th>
   357|                <th style="text-align:left">Reader's Reading</th>
   358|            </tr>
   359|            <tr>
   360|                <td><strong>Water</strong></td>
   361|                <td><span class="red-ink">Strong</span></td>
   362|                <td>Your core self — intuition, adaptability, mental depth</td>
   363|            </tr>
   364|            <tr>
   365|                <td><strong>Metal</strong></td>
   366|                <td>Moderate</td>
   367|                <td>Your source of clarity, precision, and discernment</td>
   368|            </tr>
   369|            <tr>
   370|                <td><strong>Wood</strong></td>
   371|                <td>Moderate</td>
   372|                <td>Your creativity and drive for expansion</td>
   373|            </tr>
   374|            <tr>
   375|                <td><strong>Fire</strong></td>
   376|                <td><span class="red-ink">Weak</span></td>
   377|                <td>Your visibility, social warmth, and expressive power</td>
   378|            </tr>
   379|            <tr>
   380|                <td><strong>Earth</strong></td>
   381|                <td><span class="red-ink">Weak</span></td>
   382|                <td>Your stability, discipline, and grounding force</td>
   383|            </tr>
   384|        </table>
   385|        
   386|        <div class="master-note">
   387|            <div class="master-note-header">🖋 Reader's Reading</div>
   388|            <p>You possess abundant <span class="red-ink">Water and Metal</span> energy. This makes you intellectually formidable — you see patterns, read people, and think several moves ahead. However, your weaker <span class="red-ink">Fire and Earth</span> create two challenges:</p>
   389|            <ul>
   390|                <li><strong>Fire deficiency:</strong> You may hesitate to promote yourself or speak publicly, even when you are the most qualified person in the room.</li>
   391|                <li><strong>Earth deficiency:</strong> You generate ideas constantly, but may struggle to finish one project before starting the next.</li>
   392|            </ul>
   393|            <p>These are not flaws. They are simply the terrain of your life. A wise sailor does not curse the wind; he learns to adjust his sails.</p>
   394|        </div>
   395|    </div>
   396|
   397|    <!-- PAGE 5: PERSONALITY -->
   398|    <div class="page">
   399|        <div class="section-header">Character</div>
   400|        <div class="chapter-title">Personality & Nature</div>
   401|        
   402|        <h3>Your Natural Strengths</h3>
   403|        <ol>
   404|            <li><span class="emphasis">Analytical Depth</span> — You do not accept easy answers. You enjoy reaching the root of a problem, even when the surface solution would suffice.</li>
   405|            <li><span class="emphasis">Emotional Perception</span> — You often sense what others are feeling before they speak it. This makes you a natural counselor, negotiator, or strategist.</li>
   406|            <li><span class="emphasis">Strategic Patience</span> — Unlike Fire-dominant people who rush to action, you are willing to wait for the right moment. You do not force outcomes.</li>
   407|        </ol>
   408|        
   409|        <h3>Your Recurring Blind Spots</h3>
   410|        <ol>
   411|            <li><span class="emphasis">Analysis Paralysis</span> — Your gift for deep thinking can become a prison. You may delay action until you feel "certain," and certainty rarely arrives.</li>
   412|            <li><span class="emphasis">Emotional Absorption</span> — Because you read others so well, you can absorb their stress. Chaotic social environments drain you quickly.</li>
   413|            <li><span class="emphasis">Reluctance to Self-Promote</span> — You may believe that good work speaks for itself. In most worlds, it does not. You must learn to make your value visible.</li>
   414|        </ol>
   415|        
   416|        <div class="handwritten-box">
   417|            In the classical texts, Ren Water seated on Chen Earth (your Day Pillar) is called "The River Meets the Reservoir." You have depth, but you also have containment. This means that when you find the right environment — the right team, the right city, the right partner — you can accumulate tremendous power. But in the wrong environment, you feel dammed up, restless, and out of place.
   418|        </div>
   419|    </div>
